    "answer": "The Northwatch Regiment originated in 1712 when three independent Northwatch companies were raised at Dunbrae to guard the hill roads. In 1718, two more companies joined them, supported by Captain Sera Brannoch. In 1720, these five companies were officially mustered as the Northwatch Regiment. Local speakers called the regiment \"An Freiceadan Gorm,\" which translates to \"the Blue Watch,\" because of their dark blue coats.",
